# repo-scan-public-addresses — mail addresses and Message-IDs that upstream has
# already published, which devtools/repo-scan therefore lets through (BRIEF §7,
# "What upstream has already published is public"; operator, 2026-10-13).
#
#   @domain    every address at exactly that domain (lists, list hosts, and the
#              hosts whose Message-IDs we cite)
#   address    that address, alone or at the end of a Message-ID that embeds it
#              after "-" or "." (git send-email IDs)
#
# Add an entry when a public upstream record (a lore or patchwork mail, a commit
# trailer, a stable review) carries the address. Never add a private
# correspondent: the scan's refusal of unlisted addresses is what keeps those
# out. The project author's own address is allowed by repo-scan already.

